WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
Soapy water in a glass
looks perfectly clear.

2
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:06.950
Stretch it into a thin
film across a wire loop,

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.280
light it with white light, and
bands of different shades appear.

4
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:14.590
Blow a bubble, and they
swirl across its surface.

5
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.800
Change the angle you view
it from, and they shift.

6
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:22.880
So where do those vivid hues come from,
when neither soap nor water has any of

7
00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:23.980
its own?

8
00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:28.010
In this mission, you'll find out
what happens to light at a boundary,

9
00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.990
and when a reflected wave flips over.

10
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:35.130
Then you'll see how a coating on a
camera lens cuts its reflections.

11
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:39.630
Your mission: explain where the swirling
bands on a soap bubble come from.
